 "note": "P1 (structural, finding either way): every benchmark parses with 0 bad_key and 0 degenerate and has a single dominant option count covering >=95% of valid rows, so gold position is well defined. P2 (directional headline, finding either way): exam-sourced MMLU's whole-'all' gold-position distribution is rejected as uniform at alpha=0.001 while crowd-authored OpenBookQA -- which leaks via answer LENGTH (audit 51) -- is NOT, a length-vs-position dissociation. P3 (exploitability, finding either way): among the five benchmarks MMLU has the largest 'best constant position minus chance' gap. The chi-square statistic and df are reported so an exact p-value can be recomputed; 'best_position_accuracy' is the accuracy of always guessing the single most frequent gold position. Measures construction, not any model."
